think Surveyed the live edge -- the Scooter/Dexter terminal family capstone just closed, and Season G open-media (color, the full ASCII+Latin font family, intra/inter video frames) all stand GREEN; crypto stands WHOLE (do not reopen).
think Balance-first: the font and terminal lanes have been climbed very heavily this week; a harmony-conscious lap moves to an underserved-but-high-Lindy gap rather than accreting one more font variant.
think Found a real gap in the color floor: image/color.rye owns WCAG relative_luminance + contrast_ratio_x100, yet nothing composes contrast into a decision, and no module outside color.rye references it. The single most-reached-for accessibility helper -- pick legible ink for a fill -- was missing.
think Chose readable_ink(bg) (black-or-white by higher contrast), best_ink(bg, a, b) (palette-pair generalization), and meets_aa / meets_aa_large / meets_aaa (named WCAG 2.x bars 4.50 / 3.00 / 7.00 on the existing x100 scale). Lindy-durable (accessibility is a decades-stable standard), small, and pure -- no key, no network, no funds.
think Rota item 10 (foundations/20260703-182612_sameness-is-the-macro.md) fit the lap: the new verbs are public readings of the SAME proven contrast_ratio_x100, not new math -- sameness as the macro, a page of prose not a private dialect.
obs TAME held: split every compound assert (tame_style_check bans assert(a and b)), >=2 positive asserts per fn, u8/u32 widths, no seam cast, ASCII additions (existing header keeps British colour + non-ASCII middots; not swept, narrow scope).
obs Mid-grey #666666 on white computes to 5.74:1 by the module's own integer path -- passes AA-normal (>=4.50), fails AAA (>=7.00) -- proven, not asserted from memory; the boundary #767676 was avoided as too near for integer rounding.
obs Witness extended in the same round: two new grep assertions (readable-ink pick, AA/AAA split); the four elder substrings kept intact so the proof only grew.
